<title>CANADA: StatsCan survey sees Jan unemployment at 9.7 pct.</title>
<headline>StatsCan survey sees Jan unemployment at 9.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Statistics Canada survey of analysts forecast Canadian unemployment to remain flat at 9.7 percent in January from December.</p>
<p>The survey also forecast that consumer prices would rise in January by 2.0 pct from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The survey forecast gross domestic product to rise 0.3 percent in December from November.</p>
<p>The economists also forecast merchandise exports for December at C$22.7 billion, and imports of C$20.5 billion.</p>
<p>The agency on average surveys 17 economists each month.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
